From: crackerjacques <jack@supremeoverlordjabs.co>
Subject: [PATCH] usb: musb: gadget: do not log a dequeue of an unqueued request as an error

musb_gadget_dequeue() prints "request %p not queued to %s" at error
level when asked to dequeue a request that is not on the endpoint's
list. That condition is a documented return value of usb_ep_dequeue()
(-EINVAL), not a fault: function drivers call it without knowing
whether the request already completed. u_serial's console teardown does
exactly that - it dequeues its console request unconditionally - so on
a board whose serial console is the CDC-ACM gadget the message appears
on every host detach, at KERN_ERR, on the panel that is the board's only
other console.

Drop it to dev_dbg. The return value is unchanged.

Signed-off-by: crackerjacques <jack@supremeoverlordjabs.co>
---
diff --git a/drivers/usb/musb/musb_gadget.c b/drivers/usb/musb/musb_gadget.c
index 56ffd5e2ab26..416b79bf50da 100644
--- a/drivers/usb/musb/musb_gadget.c
+++ b/drivers/usb/musb/musb_gadget.c
@@ -1301,7 +1301,7 @@ static int musb_gadget_dequeue(struct usb_ep *ep, struct usb_request *request)
 			break;
 	}
 	if (r != req) {
-		dev_err(musb->controller, "request %p not queued to %s\n",
+		dev_dbg(musb->controller, "request %p not queued to %s\n",
 				request, ep->name);
 		status = -EINVAL;
 		goto done;
